Changelog: 14-11-2026 01:05:10

Fixed. The tests, their fixture and the examples no longer name the suite for Windows devices (owner, 14-11-2026):
the second suite in the tests is "ws", with ws- tags and a windows_portal package. Nothing works differently.

Changelog: 14-11-2026 00:36:00

Added. Remove suite on the Test on this board tab: a terminal lists what of the suite is installed on this machine
and whether a test put it there, then removes every app, the portal and Bazzite Test (check-release.sh remove). Test
Portal release tests the portal's draft while the release is not published, and a test on a machine without the
suite removes what it installed when the portal closes.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 23:28:59

Added. The release tab's nine steps work in this repository: Start new release starts release.yml here, on the
release commit, and the run, the Device test of the portal's draft, Publish and the pin commit follow as steps 6 to
9. A repository that is one suite itself counts as that suite, so the Contents tab lists its apps and portal with the
versions offered. Publish makes the portal GitHub's Latest release. The tabs 1. Release apps and 2. Pin and release
Portal still publish one release by hand: a workflow that is only started, not run on a tag, leaves them as they were.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 23:12:13

Fixed. The release tab no longer shows every step with a green ✓ after a push in a repository without a release
workflow on GitHub. Steps 5 to 9 need that workflow; without it the tab found nothing to release and marked them
done, while apps had changed since their releases. Steps 1 to 4 get their ✓ as before, 5 to 9 stay gray, and the line
under the steps says the releases are made on the tabs 1. Release apps and 2. Pin and release Portal, and which apps
and portal changed since their last release.

Changelog: 13-11-2026 21:54:15

Fixed. The app's tests pass again (58 of 155 failed or stopped in their fixtures since the suite got its own tooling
back), and tools/ci-local.sh runs them. The files of a suite with tools of its own, which the tests copy into their
fixtures, are back in tests/fixtures/windows-suite/. The fixtures' suites without a TAG_PREFIX are read with this
checkout's manifest tools, which ask for ps5-: in the tests they take a tag with or without it (tests/conftest.py),
and the fixtures' apps name a category, as this suite's apps.toml must. The fixtures hold the suite's own core
(core/bazzite_console_core, what the tool looks at for a core change) instead of nexus_core, the test of a suite's
name and icon reads this checkout, and the tag button's test expects the hint the button gives ("Nothing to
publish"). The tool itself is unchanged, apart from one docstring that named the wrong core folder.

